  "notes": "Agricultural society (fair/speedway), FYE Oct 31 2025, modeled as GAAP governmental funds (General Fund subfunds Fair, Speedway, Concessions, Restricted); no business-type funds. Receipts/disbursements are the Total (General Fund) column of the Statement of Activities and Governmental Fund Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (p2-p3), not the government-wide column (which adds depreciation 41,563 and removes capital outlay). Expenditures 926,856 as printed; revenues have no single printed total, reported total = 792,771 program revenues + 133,507 taxes + 655 interest = 926,933 (computed). Roll-forward: 250,545 + 926,933 - 926,856 = 250,622 (excess 77 printed). Internal transfers (Fair -9,295, Speedway +33,443, Concessions -20,000, Restricted -4,148) net to zero in the total column, so top-level transfers are null. Transfer cross-check: transfers between funds sum to 0 (-9,295+33,443-20,000-4,148), no unmatched or hidden transfers; the Fair capital improvements 17,655 shown as other use on p6 is the same as Capital outlay on p2 (not a transfer). beginning_cash 246,258 is the cash balance beginning of year from the cash-basis budgetary schedule (p4), ending_cash 251,640 computed from the balance sheet lines (equals p4 ending cash). Balance sheet from the Statement of Net Position column (p1; no separate government-wide statement of net position). Detail: per-fund Comparative Statements (p5-6, 2025 columns used; 2024 ignored) are recorded as the more detailed schedule; the cash-basis General Fund budget schedule (p4, budget vs actual in broader groups) is not recorded in detail to avoid double counting; its totals receipts 931,253 and disbursements 925,871 are on a cash basis and differ from the GAAP statements. The Grandstand and Carnival schedule (p7) is a sub-breakdown of Fair revenue/expenses (e.g. ticket income 49,173; total revenues 131,189; expenditures 104,650) and is not recorded to avoid double counting. Taxes line not broken down anywhere, kept as taxes (unlabeled). Read pages 1-7 of 7"
}
